{"c":[{"id":"38f3f2c9b5605d54","sum":"SumMem@78d91b7: one root store, no scopes. #116: user-observable break; no exclusion lists; no second definition. #118 rules/txrk9-basic-pr-review/SKILL.md: actions not tool ids; Other=closed hunt + split-confidence omit; silence after cull; not merged with pr-feedback-judge.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"161e94da3b50d407","sum":"SumMem@78d91b7: one repo-root store, no scoped stores. always-tdd/preflight scope (#116): product-delivered or product-runtime behavior a product user would observe breaking; no tool or category exclusion lists (they get relabeled); no second definition in preflight.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"7d52b47ec9e85065","sum":"SumMem@78d91b7: one repo-root store; no scoped stores. TDD/preflight judge product-delivered or product-runtime behavior, not whatever a package manager or Actions runner executes (#116); prefer one steering principle over a tool exclusion list.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260820T203140Z-2cd50a583de58b13","text":"SumMem installed from Texarkanine/SumMem@78d91b7; one store only (repo-root .summem). Do not start scoped stores.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260820T203952Z-b85700bde1651227","text":"TDD/preflight must judge product-delivered or product-runtime behavior, not whatever a package manager or Actions runner executes (#116). Prefer one steering principle over an exclusion list of tools.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"4caf0939404591cd","sum":"always-tdd scope (#116): the product's executable behavior, judged by whether a product user would observe the break. No excluded-tool or category lists (they get relabeled, lint is a CLI); no second definition echoed into preflight.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260820T204108Z-bdc4405c71cbf0c8","text":"always-tdd in-scope is the product's executable behavior; delete 'If something executes it'. Do not list excluded tools or echo a second definition into preflight (#116).","type":"note"},{"name":"20260820T204616Z-1620ce6f602992b6","text":"Category lists in always-tdd get relabeled (lint is a CLI). Scope by 'would a user of the product observe the break' matches the change-detector test; #116 shipped the smaller 'product's executable behavior' prefix instead.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c19949f5dfc60d8e","sum":"#116/#117 tdd: bug-fixes/20260820-tdd-product-scope.md. #118 txrk9: rules/txrk9-basic-pr-review/SKILL.md, features/20260824-txrk9-pr-review.md. Names actions, not tool ids. Other=closed hunt + split-confidence omit; silence only after cull; do not merge with pr-feedback-judge.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"5202cd818d3f1b9a","sum":"tdd-product-scope archived as bug-fixes/20260820-tdd-product-scope.md (#116, PR #117). txrk9-pr-review: Other sensitivity is a closed hunt plus a split confidence omit; silence is success only after that cull; do not merge with pr-feedback-judge.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260820T204959Z-dd7f3dfe96e57256","text":"Archived tdd-product-scope as bug-fixes/20260820-tdd-product-scope.md (#116 / PR #117). One-sentence always-tdd steer; niko-preflight untouched; live proof is the next lint-only or invoke-only-CI preflight.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260824T194427Z-3aac0651e5d3eb24","text":"txrk9-pr-review: Other sensitivity is a closed hunt plus a split confidence omit; silence is success only after that cull. Do not merge with pr-feedback-judge.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b6d65b1dc5295d16","sum":"pr-review skill names posting actions, not Cursor tool identifiers. txrk9-pr-review archived as features/20260824-txrk9-pr-review.md; skill is rules/txrk9-basic-pr-review/SKILL.md (PR #118).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260824T200408Z-46497ed70935ab07","text":"pr-review skill names posting actions, not Cursor tool identifiers.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260824T203402Z-5b4dd72596686af3","text":"Archived txrk9-pr-review as memory-bank/archive/features/20260824-txrk9-pr-review.md; skill is rules/txrk9-basic-pr-review/SKILL.md (PR #118).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c74f45f04bbfcbef","sum":"L4 preflight keys on progress.md Level 4, not milestones.md; sub-runs keep the L2/L3 bar; Step 2a deletes tasks.md+progress.md. always-tdd: in=user-observable breakage (preflight FAILs on it); out=repo bootstrap; eval rules stay TDD (#123). Niko refs in rulesets/niko/skills/.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"722003b2a2f2f406","sum":"niko-core stays; Progress Tracking out. L4 preflight: progress.md Level 4, not milestones.md. Sub-runs keep milestones.md, L2/L3 TDD bar. Done/risks/refs: milestones.md or projectbrief.md; Step 2a deletes tasks.md and progress.md. L2/L3 share a bar; L4 sibling in niko-preflight.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"f2c538954be02f23","sum":"niko-core stays when a workflow restates it. Progress Tracking stays out of niko-core; task lists are Niko-workflow only. L4 preflight dispatches on progress.md Complexity Level 4, not milestones.md: sub-runs keep milestones.md and still need the L2/L3 TDD bar.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260903T020823Z-863b2cb139a2db13","text":"niko-core is the omnipresent baseline: do not strip it because a workflow restates the same idea. Progress Tracking stays out of niko-core — task lists are Niko-workflow only.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260912T163802Z-128a4d11c5b57281","text":"L4 preflight must dispatch on progress.md Complexity Level 4, not milestones.md presence: sub-runs keep milestones.md and still need the L2/L3 TDD bar.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b0930c512db1fec0","sum":"L4 done, risks, and ticket refs live in milestones.md or projectbrief.md: Step 2a deletes tasks.md and progress.md. Preflight and QA are spawnable, one-line bootstrap, not routers. L2 and L3 share one preflight bar; L4 is a sibling reference in niko-preflight.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260912T163805Z-74c7fba4792433f6","text":"L4 per-milestone done, risks, and ticket refs must live in milestones.md or projectbrief.md: /niko Step 2a deletes tasks.md and progress.md before later milestones run.","type":"note"},{"name":"20260912T164808Z-b70c7feb534b80b1","text":"Preflight and QA stay spawnable skills with a one-line Run the skill bootstrap; they are not plan/build workflow routers. L2 and L3 share one preflight bar; L4 is a sibling reference inside niko-preflight.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"8a11870eed5512b0","sum":"always-tdd: in-scope=user-observable breakage, preflight FAILs on that not plan label; out=repo bootstrap, not agent prompts; rules w/ evals stay TDD (#123). Niko skill refs in rulesets/niko/skills/; topic skills in rules/, symlinked. L4 Execution Order serial-safe; charts agree.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"c38cc7df7755cb76","sum":"always-tdd in-scope is user-observable breakage; preflight FAILs on that test, not the plan label (#123). Niko workflow skills keep references/ beside SKILL.md under rulesets/niko/skills/; topic skills live under rules/ and symlink into a ruleset.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260912T165056Z-1e3c090a0fc2764f","text":"always-tdd in-scope is behavior a user of this product can observe breaking (no CLI/workflow category list). Preflight classifies and FAILs on that test, not the plan's executable label (#123).","type":"note"},{"name":"20260912T170355Z-1e7e525d29c37eed","text":"Niko workflow skills keep references/ beside SKILL.md under rulesets/niko/skills/; topic skills still live under rules/ and symlink into a ruleset.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"9969d0d4099ef039","sum":"always-tdd out-of-scope is repository bootstrap (AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, copied init), not agent-facing prompts; rules with evals stay TDD (#123). L4 Execution Order is a serial-safe list; a flowchart's parallel sets must agree with it.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20260912T171208Z-73d07cf3ecfc8407","text":"always-tdd out-of-scope is repository bootstrap (AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, copied init), not agent-facing prompts; product rules with evals would still be TDD (#123 rework).","type":"note"},{"name":"20260912T175124Z-ed6de308b249777f","text":"L4 Execution Order: the checklist is always a serial-safe walk (one-at-a-time never needs a later milestone); when work is not a line, the flowchart records parallel sets. Follow the list or the DAG; they must agree so a mid-project switch does not conflict.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
